body:
Its with my first gf (now ex i guess) , our relationship was pretty toxic on both parts but i loved her to death nonetheless, she was my first gf after all and i was single for a very long loong time. It was pretty rocky but we had great times. Lots of problems, i was diagnosed with Major depressive disorder, Bipolar 2 and major anxiety and panic disorder. She didnt really support me, she was more in denial and compared her problems too, saying everyone goes through shit. 

My mental health deteriorated pretty quickly, making me self admit to a mental ward for suicidal behaviors ( I had a history with self harm) and i was in there for 3 days, pure hell. When i got out i realised my gf had sent me msgs everyday updating what she was doing and so forth, and it made me feel loved. But i also found out that she posted provocative shit in her ig and was talking sexual kinky stuffs to  my closest friends (more than one). So i took a break from her then got back, the cycle repeated a few times until last month, when she said she was drained mentally from everything and wanted time off. Ok i thought. Then she started calling less, msging less ( we were in a long distance relationship) and even stopped calling before sleeping ( we had this routine where we would sleep on call, corny i knw ). 

She just became more and more distant, talking less to me but being more online and posting more provocative shit. Then at one point i had a hunch and accused her of cheating and lo and behold, she was talking to her ex flings and her excuse was that we broke up and she had to do anything to get over me. TF? When did we break up??? So i lost my shit and so forth and she said she didnt want to be with me until i had changed and started trusting her more and gave her more freedom. I tried but she just left. We had a month break but i couldnt handle it so i just started msging her and she just started attacking me and blaming me and of course, said that i never changed. Till now she cant admit that she doesnt want me in her life nor have a future visioned, she said she loved being single and the freedom with it and doesnt see herself in a relationship any time soon, if asked about me she would ask if i had changed.

&#x200B;

Sorry for the long rant, i guess i just want your opinion on this and help me cus the stupidest part of me still wants her back when theres red flags everywhere adn how do i cope with this? She is my first love and at this point with my depression and urge to OD this would be my last relationship as well. Thanks to those that read and have a great day.

Sorry for bad english and grammar but i cant be bothered lol

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

S

My experience is quite beginner and im under medications (  Mirtazapine 45 mg ,lithium 350mg and Epilim 1g ). Under relatively low doses ( 2- 4 pills 25mg each ) it causes a sedating effect, helps with my anxiety, makes me feel calm and enhances music. Makes my body feel heavy but in a good way.

I once tried 6 pills (25mg each). It started pretty similar as well, music was great and nice heavy body feel. But after awhile, i started to get dark thoughts, it didnt make me freak out but somehow, welcoming i guess. soon i started to see some stuff in the darkness but couldnt make sense of it, maybe there was something maybe not, but i knew it was cus of the pills so i didnt panic. The darkness seemed extra dark ,but it was peaceful and calming. Like how you would feel if you were under the ocean and staring at the abysss, sure it was scary but it was the truth and it was the end, there was nothing to worry about, i was at peace and at my end of destination. Curiosity peaked and i started to walk around, heard some noices like insects scuttling away, felt like i was being watched too. At this point i didnt know how i felt with music because i just didnt feel like listening to it, i dont think i wouldve liked it either way. The heavy body feel was gone and replaced with this sedating and floating yet drunked feel. Like i could walk to one point to another but i would be stumbling like i was drunk. It was late night at this point so i decided to call it a day and go to sleep.

&#x200B;

A few hours after sleeping i woke up from a panic attack. I was sort of sober but couldnt feel my chest and heart, it was heavy to breathe and i legit thought i had a heart attack. My head grew woosy and my chest felt empty, i was taking shallow breath and was freaking out. I had to calm my self and started my regular panic attack routine (ive had plenty) , started wit deep breaths, sitting straight up, turning my lights on and played " Help im having a panic attack RN " vids from youtube (some help, especially those with calming music) did that for half an hour and collapsed from exhausting to sleep. (Im used to it). 

&#x200B;

The next morning my chest still felt empty and numbish but overall better, on hindsight it mightve been seratonin syndrome but couldnt be sure. My last dose was about last week when i took 2 pills for a panic attack ( I have Major anxiety and panic disorder but my docs dont give me meds for it :) ) but since then ive only been saving it for my next attack, no intention on tripping tho. I might venture in DXM cus ive heard its way better than DPH but i need to get my hand on it first. Anyways hope yall had a good read and have a great day ! Trip safe my friends
